# AI, rendering, and licence safety

- Model output is validated with `validatePlan` (ARCHITECTURE §6.1) and compiled by trusted templates. Never eval it, never put it in innerHTML, attributes, CSS, URLs, or paths. Escape all text.
- Visual facts come from traces, measured audio, or creator data. The model never writes data-structure values or timestamps.
- User code runs only in the browser worker (Pyodide / QuickJS) with step, time, depth, and size caps. The server only validates trace JSON.
- Providers only through adapters and the quota router. Record usage. Voices never fall back silently. Projects with `keepPrivate` never reach providers that train on free-tier input.
- Every file in `library/` has a `manifest.json` row with licence and credit. Banned sources: unDraw, DrawKit, Blush, Storyset, Freesound API, MusicGen weights, edge-tts, Coqui XTTS.
- No copyrighted characters, real-person likeness, or voice cloning.
- Renders are deterministic: local fonts and libraries, seeded randomness, no network at render time.
